s and against three shipping Developer ID packet-tunnel products installed on this Mac before being accepted; all four confirmed. F1 NE values are now keyed by signing channel (development=packet-tunnel-provider, developer-id=packet-tunnel-provider-systemextension) with C1 pinned to the development set. F2 App Groups moved to the registered iOS-style literal on both platforms. F3 assertion A10 replaced by four assertions over a computed authored-vs-signing-generated allowlist. F4 App Sandbox attributed per requirementSource - provider apple-requirement, host project-architecture. Gates: validate_matrix.py 537 checks exit 0; mutate.py 23/23 negative gates exit 0; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0. Both harness scripts verified to run in place from the board resource layout. No board elements created or changed. New OC-4 records the one unverified corner: no Apple source confirms an iOS-style app group ID works as a sandboxed Mach service name prefix; owned by TASK-260728-7ii1xz, not blocking because the spec host-to-provider channel is not XPC.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-39e294, pid=43034, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-fdc95a, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-fdc95a)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-fdc95a, pid=57550, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-641408, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-641408)\nr3 rework against reviewer verdict 02 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1). The finding was independently re-verified before acceptance and CONFIRMED three ways: .spec/platform-distribution.md:103-105 mandates the Sparkle -spks/-spki Mach lookup exceptions for the sandboxed host; this repo own .research/260721_macos-self-update.md:111-113 records the identical two-value set; and codesign -d --entitlements :- across /Applications found six shipping apps carrying exactly that pattern, three of them sandboxed with those two values and nothing else. Fix: macos.host now authors com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name as required-adjacent with the exact authored array plus a resolvedValue for bundle-level checking, portalCapability false, owner uyju7n, project-architecture attribution (attributionNote states why it is not sandbox-consequence, unlike network.client). Rule X1 added because the same spec clause bans unreviewed exception entitlements: a reviewed-exception register plus a banned set for Hardened Runtime relaxations, with get-task-allow deliberately left to A10d. Assertions A10e, A14, A15 added; R27 pins the assertion id set so it cannot silently shrink again. Two evidence notes recorded rather than smoothed over: Tailscale ships the exception while unsandboxed (so shipping-product presence is not proof of requirement), and Sparkle binary names three endpoint suffixes (-spks, -spki, -spkp) of which only two are entitled, making the two-value set deliberate. Gates: reviewer own targeted jq gate now true/exit 0 (was false/exit 1); validate_matrix.py 27 rules 598 checks exit 0; mutate.py 41/41 negative gates exit 0; 11/11 explicit r2-preservation assertions hold; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. Both harness scripts re-verified running in place from the board resource layout. No board elements created or changed; no product source, spec, or generated project modified.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-641408, pid=58959, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-8b59cc, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-8b59cc)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-8b59cc, pid=62847, exit=0)\n2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz AMENDMENT REQUEST (this task is the applying owner per matrix section 11). Verdict: keychain-access-groups on works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel KEEP PROHIBITED - promote prohibited-pending-decision to settled prohibited. The selected transport is the file-based System keychain, whose access model is per-item SecAccess ACLs, not access groups (TN3137), so the entitlement is inapplicable rather than merely unused. The provider needs no keychain entitlement: /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb lines 792-793 on macOS 26.5 25F71 already grant read+write on /Library/Keychains to any process holding com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension, and lines 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No new entitlement, App ID, portal 